WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.780
(orchestral music)

00:00:02.780 --> 00:00:06.910
- [Sasha] When I'm out on
a wakeboard, it feels free,

00:00:06.910 --> 00:00:09.693
like I am able to do what I want.

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:11.790
I'm Sasha Christian,

00:00:11.790 --> 00:00:13.333
and I'm Singapore's
number one wakeboarder.

00:00:14.512 --> 00:00:17.429
(orchestral music)

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:26.050
- [Narrator] Sasha is Singapore's

00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:27.913
first Asian wakeboarding champion.

00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:30.800
She started water sports at a young age,

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:34.010
and at 5 years old,
wakeboarding caught her eye.

00:00:34.010 --> 00:00:35.790
- [Sasha] I went for my
first wakeboard competition

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:37.050
when I was 11 years old.

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:39.630
It was the Asian
championships held in China,

00:00:39.630 --> 00:00:41.750
and I got third that year.

00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:44.330
In 2009, it was a big year for me

00:00:44.330 --> 00:00:46.020
because I won the Asian championship,

00:00:46.020 --> 00:00:48.540
so I was Asian champion for that year.

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:50.183
I now 16 then.

00:00:51.490 --> 00:00:53.195
Growing up as a female wakeboarder

00:00:53.195 --> 00:00:56.040
most of the people I wakeboarded
with were mostly guys,

00:00:56.040 --> 00:00:57.510
you know, my brother included.

00:00:57.510 --> 00:00:58.610
But that was actually really good,

00:00:58.610 --> 00:01:01.360
because they pushed me really hard,

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:03.080
you know, they didn't cut me any slack.

00:01:03.080 --> 00:01:04.060
And so, because of that,

00:01:04.060 --> 00:01:06.060
it made me a better wakeboarder as well.

00:01:12.230 --> 00:01:15.260
The hardest thing about
wakeboarding would be

00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:18.010
pushing yourself when you're afraid.

00:01:18.010 --> 00:01:21.000
Pushing through that fear
is one of the hardest things

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:22.743
but also the most rewarding thing.

00:01:23.970 --> 00:01:25.130
- [Narrator] Today Sasha trains

00:01:25.130 --> 00:01:28.080
Singapore's next generation
of female wakeboarders.

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:30.060
She's eager to push others to succeed

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:31.573
in the same ways she did.

00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:35.850
- [Sasha] One of my
biggest goal for this year

00:01:35.850 --> 00:01:39.870
is to help to grow the
wakeboard scene in Singapore

00:01:39.870 --> 00:01:43.580
and to see the women
keep pushing the standard

00:01:43.580 --> 00:01:44.683
on what we have here.

00:01:45.640 --> 00:01:48.540
It's important not to
set limits for ourselves.

00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:49.650
When there's something
out there you want to do,

00:01:49.650 --> 00:01:52.050
or you want to achieve,

00:01:52.050 --> 00:01:53.443
don't let anything stand in your way.

00:01:53.443 --> 00:01:55.450
There's a way to achieve that.

00:01:55.450 --> 00:01:57.222
Don't let anyone else tell you otherwise.

00:01:57.222 --> 00:02:00.139
(orchestral music)

